(3339033, 461889, 66952, '<td valign="top">I like the composition quite a lot, the kids playing by themselves and in pairs at the corners of the image. The biggest problem with the image is the colors look a bit oversaturated and yellow. A smaller problem is the bicycle (or whatever it is) in the corner. Maybe you could have taken a step closer to the girl, to be able to crop out the bike.</td>', 'I like the composition quite a lot, the kids playing by themselves and in pairs at the corners of the image. The biggest problem with the image is the colors look a bit oversaturated and yellow. A smaller problem is the bicycle (or whatever it is) in the corner. Maybe you could have taken a step closer to the girl, to be able to crop out the bike.', '2007-02-07 10:52:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(3339052, 462394, 66952, '<td valign="top">This is a nice skyline picture, and it certainly fits within the challenge. It just doesn''t quite work, though, because of the colors and contrast. There''s a little too much contrast, and the colors are way too oversaturated.</td>', 'This is a nice skyline picture, and it certainly fits within the challenge. It just doesn''t quite work, though, because of the colors and contrast. There''s a little too much contrast, and the colors are way too oversaturated.', '2007-02-07 10:56:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(3339063, 464209, 13207, '<td valign="top">And still two trolls!</td>', 'And still two trolls!', '2007-02-07 10:59:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(3339067, 464948, 66952, '<td valign="top">A good idea, but the lighting doesn''t work. The flowers need to have more light, especially towards the back, where they''re lost in shadow. It would work better to be able to see the contrast of the flowers against the dark background. To get this to work, you''ll need to pull the subject several feet away from the background, then light just the subject. Put a piece of cloth or something between the light and the background, to keep the background dark.</td>', 'A good idea, but the lighting doesn''t work. The flowers need to have more light, especially towards the back, where they''re lost in shadow. It would work better to be able to see the contrast of the flowers against the dark background. To get this to work, you''ll need to pull the subject several feet away from the background, then light just the subject. Put a piece of cloth or something between the light and the background, to keep the background dark.', '2007-02-07 11:00:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(3339086, 464502, 66952, '<td valign="top">I really like this image, and the feeling it evokes. I''m not sure if a (little) tighter crop would work better or not. I''m sure you tried it, so I''ll try not to second guess, but for 640x, I might like to see more bird detail.</td>', 'I really like this image, and the feeling it evokes. I''m not sure if a (little) tighter crop would work better or not. I''m sure you tried it, so I''ll try not to second guess, but for 640x, I might like to see more bird detail.', '2007-02-07 11:07:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(3339096, 465049, 66952, '<td valign="top">Totally cool. Most people just took a shot of something and gave it a "good" title. You actually came up with a concept. Extra points for that. The lighting may be a little flat. Both kids, especially the boy, could use some backlighting to separate them from the background, but it''s still cool.</td>', 'Totally cool. Most people just took a shot of something and gave it a "good" title. You actually came up with a concept. Extra points for that. The lighting may be a little flat. Both kids, especially the boy, could use some backlighting to separate them from the background, but it''s still cool.', '2007-02-07 11:10:51.000000', NULL, 1),
