(3364705, 462996, 51750, '<td valign="top">A very good photograph, i knew it would be up at the top by the end. Im not really sure how you achieved this picture legally though because the dynamic range seems very high.</td>', 'A very good photograph, i knew it would be up at the top by the end. Im not really sure how you achieved this picture legally though because the dynamic range seems very high.', '2007-02-14 09:26:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(3364754, 463932, 48471, '<td valign="top">Thanks for having a look at this photo. Believe me, it''s better than you think...well, if you don''t believe me, than just think about it...anyway.<br/>This photo is good just because it has no subject, no golden sun, no islands, no silhouettes, no beaches...it''s just our planet, wrongly named Earth...<br/>And, what the hell does Planet Ocean cares if some hairless monkeys start feeling hot?</td>', 'Thanks for having a look at this photo. Believe me, it''s better than you think...well, if you don''t believe me, than just think about it...anyway.This photo is good just because it has no subject, no golden sun, no islands, no silhouettes, no beaches...it''s just our planet, wrongly named Earth...And, what the hell does Planet Ocean cares if some hairless monkeys start feeling hot?', '2007-02-14 09:33:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(3364853, 462996, 30807, '<td valign="top">A beautiful Photograph of a lovely place, well worth an award. I wish I had taken it. I think a graduated filter at the top of the picture (I am assuming you used one), prevents the top being too bright, and concentrates attention on the main part of the whole. Someone said that the right hand could maybe have done with a bit brighter, which could be right. I would still like to buy a print of this picture though, and wish you the very best in your future scenic pictures<br/> <br/>Adrian</td>', 'A beautiful Photograph of a lovely place, well worth an award. I wish I had taken it. I think a graduated filter at the top of the picture (I am assuming you used one), prevents the top being too bright, and concentrates attention on the main part of the whole. Someone said that the right hand could maybe have done with a bit brighter, which could be right. I would still like to buy a print of this picture though, and wish you the very best in your future scenic pictures Adrian', '2007-02-14 09:51:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(3364882, 463480, 26045, '<td valign="top">i think this is one of the most pure photos i''ve ever seen. it''s so effortlessly joyful and clean. very, very nice...</td>', 'i think this is one of the most pure photos i''ve ever seen. it''s so effortlessly joyful and clean. very, very nice...', '2007-02-14 09:54:10.000000', NULL, 0),
