(3409350, 464962, 62318, '<td valign="top">I really like this picture. Great expressions, with your son in the middle with the slightly different pose to really give a terrific interest that is usually lacking in these shots. One of those everything is the same except one, that really makes a strong image. Also like the nice little touches of the varied colored shirts and the texture of the grass. A wonderful image.</td>', 'I really like this picture. Great expressions, with your son in the middle with the slightly different pose to really give a terrific interest that is usually lacking in these shots. One of those everything is the same except one, that really makes a strong image. Also like the nice little touches of the varied colored shirts and the texture of the grass. A wonderful image.', '2007-02-27 11:27:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(3417219, 464646, 47852, '<td valign="top">Since you posted the thread about needing more comments, I came to find your last shot that was in the range you mentioned.<br/> <br/>I like the unique composition here with the mirror only taking up a part of the shot and not being a full mirror.  The expression on your model is very warming and definately makes me smile.  The ''softness'' in the mirror is nice, but the model herself seems to be just blurry, which I find distracting.  It''s especially noticable down by her hand/chin, and the glint of that ring draws your eye into that area.  One other thing I find bothers me is the shadow from her hair that falls onto the reflection, making a large triangle on her forehead.</td>', 'Since you posted the thread about needing more comments, I came to find your last shot that was in the range you mentioned. I like the unique composition here with the mirror only taking up a part of the shot and not being a full mirror.  The expression on your model is very warming and definately makes me smile.  The ''softness'' in the mirror is nice, but the model herself seems to be just blurry, which I find distracting.  It''s especially noticable down by her hand/chin, and the glint of that ring draws your eye into that area.  One other thing I find bothers me is the shadow from her hair that falls onto the reflection, making a large triangle on her forehead.', '2007-03-01 06:12:23.000000', NULL, 0),
